-- title:
--   Diamonds with d≡ 1 mod M fix supersingular points
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M$ an integer with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$; let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ for $\{p\}$, and $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}(L)$ equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), that is, the $L$-subfield of $L((q))$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the level-$Mp$ function field $\mathbb{Q}(X_1(Mp)) \subseteq \mathbb{Q}((q))$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with an $L$-algebra structure making $L$ its fraction field, such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A$, with $A$ acting on $K$ compatibly through $L$, and let $\varpi$ generate the maximal ideal of $A$. Let $j \in K$ be nonzero with $q$-expansion the coefficientwise image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157). Write $R =$ `chartAlgFin A K j` for the subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j]$, and let $y$ be a point of $\mathrm{Spec}\,R$ whose prime ideal contains the image of $\varpi$ and is supersingular in the sense that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $p$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi \colon R \to \Omega$ with kernel $y$, the element $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet p Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), i.e. every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has no nonzero affine point killed by $p$. Let $d$ be coprime to $Mp$ with $d \equiv 1 \pmod M$, and let $\theta$ be an $L$-algebra automorphism of $K$ which on $q$-expansions agrees with the base change to $L$ of the diamond automorphism $\langle d \rangle$ of $\mathbb{Q}(X_1(Mp))$. Let $\rho \colon R \to R$ be a ring endomorphism inducing $\theta$ on elements of $K$. Then the contraction of $y$ along $\rho$ equals $y$, and $\rho(s) - s \in y$ for every $s \in R$.
--
--   This says that the automorphism of the special fibre at $p$ of the two-chart integral model of $X_1(Mp)$ induced by a diamond operator $\langle d \rangle$ with $d \equiv 1 \pmod M$ fixes each supersingular point $y$ and acts trivially on its residue field, hence fixes every geometric point above $y$ — classically, the diamonds $\langle b \rangle_p$ fix the crossings of the two Igusa components. It is used in the construction of the isomorphism of crossing data on the special fibre that compares the model with its $\langle d \rangle$-twist.
